== Chapter 3: Einstein's equation as a falling ball (Baez-Bunn)
ok  R_tt = 4 pi (rho + p_x + p_y + p_z), so Vddot/V = -4 pi (rho + sum p)
ok  perfect fluid: source rho + 3p
ok  ball keeps its volume when p = -rho/3
ok  vacuum energy p = -rho gives rho + 3p = -2 rho
ok  uniform matter: laplacian(Phi) = 4 pi rho (Poisson)
ok  Newtonian ball in dust: Vddot/V = -4 pi rho, matching the ball equation with p = 0

